{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"The peer-facing door: another peer's peerchat calls this over the peer network to hand over one message. The sender is the authenticated peer connection (nn_session.username), never anything in the payload; a non-peer session is refused. Creates the conversation on first contact, stores the message once (a repeated id is acknowledged, not stored again), counts it unread and fires the peerchat MESSAGE event. Returns OK, which the sender records as the delivery receipt. Open to the admin and peerchat groups.","groups":"peerchat","import":"use flowlang::flowlang::system::time::time as now_ms;\nuse crate::peerchat::peerchat::flush::{valid, append, messages, touch, nudge, MAX_TEXT};","params":[{"desc":"The sender's message id; a repeat of an id already stored from this sender is acknowledged without storing it again.","name":"id","type":"String"},{"desc":"The message text.","name":"text","type":"String"},{"desc":"When the sender wrote it, epoch milliseconds.","name":"time","type":"Integer"},{"desc":"Request metadata filled in by the peer transport from the authenticated connection; its username is the sending peer's uuid. Never taken from the caller's payload.","name":"nn_session","type":"JSONObject"}],"returntype":"String","type":"rust"},"id":"plnkpl1a1c708dbf1h4","readers":["peerchat"],"time":1794340646955,"username":"system","writers":[]}